// Soester Boerde — 5 km across real farmland east of Soest, and the module the
// field import is demonstrated on. Everything but the `fields:` list is a few
// lines of track: what makes it worth driving is that the countryside beside it
// is the countryside that is actually there.
//
//   cargo run -p app -- --scenario example:boerdefahrt
//
// The fields came from the Landwirtschaftskammer Nordrhein-Westfalen's InVeKoS
// service for the 2026 application year (dl-de/by-2-0, see `field_sources:` and
// THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md). Regenerate them — after a crop mapping was
// corrected, or for a later year — with the route editor's File > Import
// fields.
//
// 130 fields, 519 ha. Crops as of the import:
//    winter-cereal 62
//            maize 19
//        grassland 16
//           potato 11
//       sugar-beet 10
//         rapeseed 5
//           legume 3
//    summer-cereal 1
//        vegetable 1
//          orchard 1
//           fallow 1
